                <h4>NOTE:	CALCULATION OF ACTUAL HOURLY PRODUCTION (@S. No. 11)</h4>
                <br />
                <ol type="A">
                    <li>
                        <b>Theoretical hourly production (m3 / hour) –</b> Q = q x (60 / cm) x e x E<br />
                        <b>Soil type	=	Hard to Cut</b><br />
                        Where <br />
                        Q	=	Theoretical hourly production (m3/h)<br />
                        q	=	Production per cycle of loose soil (m3)<br />
                        cm	=	Cycle time (in minute)<br />
                        e	=	Grade factor (1 for 0 grade)<br />
                        E	=	Job efficiency (0.75 as average)<br />
                        <ol type="a">
                            <li>
                                q	=	q1 x a<br />
                                q1	=	Blade capacity (m3) [0.8 x W x H2]<br />
                                W = Width of blade (m)<br />
                                H = Height of blade (m)<br />
                                a	=	Blade factor (0.8)
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                cm	=	D/F + D/R + Z<br />
                                D	=	Haul Distance = 25 m<br />
                                F	=	Forward Speed (m/min) – <b>Bidder shall specify</b><br />
                                R	=	Reverse Speed (m/min) – <b>Bidder shall specify</b><br />
                                Z	=	Time required for gear shifting (0.08 min)
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <b>Actual hourly production =	0.8 x Q (m3 / hour)</b>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </div>
